    "Concurrent identical replies can transmit duplicate frames while written is pending. The immutable logical response and original request ID are preserved; installed OMP removes the pending resolver before resolving the first response and ignores later same-ID frames.",
    "Transport errors can follow partial or completed writes. Duplicate replay is allowed; no exactly-once byte guarantee is claimed.",
    "Pure laws constrain called Bend admission/send/failure composition and SQL construction. SQLite execution, socket binding, native PID ownership, byte delivery and provider behavior remain runtime boundaries.",
    "Surviving-owner observer recovery is covered by controlled fixtures. Keeper loss and host reboot are outside this acceptance.",
    "The real run uses a deterministic extension before_agent_start hook and deterministic parent responder. Spontaneous model questions and native-model parent judgment are outside this run.",
    "No matched old-Baton performance comparison is part of this acceptance."
